-- Enrichment Batch 43 (2026-10-30): NEW 1007 — CityUHK Outstanding Athletes Entrance
-- Scholarship (OAES) for Non-Local Students (rel 10, source 3195, link 495, side row
-- 724). The scheme surfaced on CityUHK's current Entrance Scholarship page read in
-- Pass 135 (source 3188) and is recorded as its own individually verified award
-- rather than folded into the academic entrance-scholarship record (556); duplicate
-- checks confirmed no athlete scheme and no pre-existing source. The batch's other
-- candidate was dropped on evidence: the HKSAR Belt and Road Scholarship and the
-- HKSAR Government Scholarship (Outstanding Performance) already exist as complete,
-- rel-10 records (974/975, added 2026-10-28 and explicitly documenting the
-- Uzbekistan awardee in 2024/25), so the first-hand re-read of the Study in Hong
-- Kong scholarships page in this batch added nothing and nothing was minted from it.
-- OAES terms from the page read in full today: extension of the since-1997 Student
-- Athletes Admission Scheme (1,600+ admitted) to non-local athletes; up to
-- HK$250,000 a year (the university's own approximation US$32,050 is quoted in the
-- description, not structured), described as equivalent to the Top Scholarship and
-- not stackable with the Diversity Grant; undergraduates — full tuition for the
-- normal duration (max four years) plus the Residence Scholarship (hall fees);
-- master's — full/partial tuition for one year only, no residence element; 18
-- listed sports; panel selection with recommendation to colleges for admission;
-- two-step application (admission by the 15 January 2027 main-round deadline, then
-- the OAES form by 30 January 2027 — stored as deadline_date, type fixed);
-- undergraduate renewal on satisfactory sports performance and CGPA of at least 2.5
-- (a renewal figure — not stored as min_gpa). award_amount = the published maximum
-- HK$250,000 with basis 'range' (top-of-range convention, cf. record 783);
-- amount_usd_value 0 (non-USD). Notes appends are replay-once; writes were executed
-- strictly sequentially.

